 """
 ================================================================================
-EODHD Provider — v4.15.0 (UNIT-AWARE PERCENT CONVERSION: the magnitude guess
+EODHD Provider — v4.15.1 (HTTP 402 PLAN-RESTRICTION CIRCUIT BREAKER)
+================================================================================
+
+v4.15.1 — WHY
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+The production workbook showed `fetch_failed:HTTP 402` on 9,797 rows across the
+four market pages. HTTP 402 means the requested endpoint is not available under
+the active account/plan. The provider previously treated 402 as a generic,
+per-symbol FetchError: it did not emit `provider_unhealthy:eodhd`, did not count
+the failures toward the circuit breaker, and continued repeating the same known-
+failing request thousands of times. That wasted most of the refresh window and
+left the engine with price-only fallback rows.
+
+FIX: classify HTTP 402 as PlanRestricted, emit the existing provider-unhealthy
+marker, count consecutive plan failures independently, and open the EODHD circuit
+at the same configurable threshold used for auth/IP failures. A 402 is terminal
+for the request and is never retried. The engine can therefore move immediately
+to the next provider instead of burning the batch window on an unavailable plan.
+
